IMPORT prelude

-- Variable Capital Companies Act 2018 (Singapore) -- the sole object (s 15), members' liability and the one-member
-- minimum (ss 17, 17A), the duty to refuse registration (s 18), sub-fund segregation (s 29), redemption (s 35), the
-- manager (s 46), directors (s 48) including members' liability for debts when the board is incomplete, fit and proper
-- directors (s 53), and disqualification on conviction (s 58).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/ (amendments to
-- Act 24 of 2025).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 37 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository, mostly s 2 (20) and s 58 (8). SCOPED
-- to what makes a VCC different from a company and what a director or member can be liable for. Not encoded: the
-- application of the Companies Act and IRDA (ss 5 to 6A), administration (Part 2), most of Parts 3 to 5, sub-fund winding
-- up and dissolution, debentures, charges, meetings, accounts, audit, winding up, foreign VCCs, and offences machinery.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Variable Capital Companies Act 2018 -- core`

§§ `15 -- one object only`

-- s 15(1): "The sole object of a VCC is to be one or more collective investment schemes in the form of a body corporate."
-- (2): it may not carry on, or join any arrangement to carry on, any business inconsistent with that object.
-- (3): the VCC -- $150,000 and $15,000 a day; every officer in default -- $150,000 or 2 years.
DECLARE Business IS ONE OF
    `operating a collective investment scheme`
    `investing scheme assets`
    `running a restaurant`
    `a joint venture to develop property for sale`

GIVEN `the business` IS A Business
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the business is consistent with the sole object` IF
    CONSIDER `the business`
    WHEN `operating a collective investment scheme` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `investing scheme assets` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- (Whether a property development joint venture is "inconsistent" with a property fund's scheme is a judgment the
-- text leaves open; it is shown as inconsistent here, as a business rather than an investment.)

§§ `17, 17A, 18 -- members and registration`

-- s 17(3): a member's liability "is limited to the amount (if any) unpaid on the shares held by the member", (4) without
-- affecting any other liability under the Act. s 17A: "at least one member".
-- s 18(2): the Registrar MUST refuse to register if (a) the named manager does not satisfy s 46(2); (b) "none of its
-- directors is either a director or qualified representative of the manager"; (c) it is likely to be used for an
-- unlawful or prejudicial purpose; or (d) registration would be contrary to national security or interest. (3): appeal
-- to the Minister within 30 days; the Minister's decision is final.
DECLARE Proposal HAS
    `the manager is qualified under section 46(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a director is a director or qualified representative of the manager` IS A BOOLEAN
    `likely to be used for an unlawful or prejudicial purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
    `contrary to national security or interest` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the proposal` IS A Proposal
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Registrar must refuse registration` IF
        NOT `the proposal`'s `the manager is qualified under section 46(2)`
    OR  NOT `the proposal`'s `a director is a director or qualified representative of the manager`
    OR  `the proposal`'s `likely to be used for an unlawful or prejudicial purpose`
    OR  `the proposal`'s `contrary to national security or interest`

GIVEN `unpaid on the member's shares` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the member's liability as a member` MEANS
    `unpaid on the member's shares`

§§ `29 -- sub-funds are ring-fenced`

-- s 29(1): "Despite any written law or rule of law to the contrary -- (a) the assets of a sub-fund of an umbrella VCC must
-- not be used to discharge any liability of the VCC or any other sub-fund ..., including in the winding up ...; and (b)
-- any liability of a sub-fund ... must be discharged solely out of the assets of that sub-fund".
-- (2): any provision of the constitution, an agreement, a contract "or otherwise" inconsistent with (1) is VOID, and so is
-- any application of assets in breach.
-- (3): assets and liabilities not attributable to any sub-fund may be allocated between sub-funds "in a manner that it
-- considers fair to shareholders".
-- (4): a contravention without reasonable excuse -- the VCC and every officer in default, $150,000 with intent to defraud,
-- $50,000 otherwise.
--
-- (2) makes even the VCC's own guarantee of one sub-fund's debt from another sub-fund's assets void. A creditor of
-- sub-fund A cannot take security over sub-fund B's assets, whatever the parties sign.
DECLARE Claim HAS
    `the creditor dealt with sub-fund A` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the assets sought belong to sub-fund A` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a contract purports to give recourse to another sub-fund` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the claim` IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the creditor may be paid from those assets` IF
        `the claim`'s `the creditor dealt with sub-fund A`
    AND `the claim`'s `the assets sought belong to sub-fund A`

GIVEN `the claim` IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the cross-recourse term is void` IF
    `the claim`'s `a contract purports to give recourse to another sub-fund`

-- In dollars.
GIVEN `intent to defraud` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine for breaching segregation` MEANS
    IF `intent to defraud` THEN 150000 ELSE 50000

§§ `35 -- redemption`

-- s 35(2): "A VCC must not repurchase or redeem its own shares unless they are fully paid." (4): redeemed shares must be
-- cancelled and issued capital reduced by the consideration paid. (3), (5): except for cross sub-fund investment under
-- s 31.
GIVEN `the shares are fully paid` IS A BOOLEAN, `under section 31` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the VCC may redeem the shares` IF
    `the shares are fully paid` OR `under section 31`

§§ `46 -- the manager`

-- s 46(1): a VCC "must at all times have a manager". (2): (a) a capital markets services licensee for fund management,
-- (c) a person in s 99(1)(a) to (d) of the Securities and Futures Act 2001 (exempt persons such as banks), or (d) a
-- prescribed person. (3): "A VCC cannot be its own manager." (4): a SUSPENDED licence does not count.
DECLARE ManagerCandidate IS ONE OF
    `a licensed fund manager`
    `a fund manager whose licence is suspended`
    `a bank exempt under section 99(1)`
    `the VCC itself`
    `an unlicensed adviser`

GIVEN `the candidate` IS A ManagerCandidate
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the candidate may be the VCC's manager` IF
    CONSIDER `the candidate`
    WHEN `a licensed fund manager` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a bank exempt under section 99(1)` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `48 -- directors, and members who become liable for debts`

-- s 48(1): at least one director ordinarily resident in Singapore, and at least one who is a director or qualified
-- representative of the manager (may be the same person). (2): natural persons, at least 18, of full capacity.
-- (5), (6): a director "must not resign or vacate his or her office" unless those two requirements are still met after;
-- a resignation in breach "is invalid". (7): except on disqualification or removal.
-- (11): if the VCC "carries on business for more than 6 months without" those directors, "a person who ... (c) is a
-- MEMBER of the VCC; and (d) KNOWS that the VCC is carrying on business in that manner, is liable for the payment of ALL
-- THE DEBTS of the VCC contracted during the period" after the 6 months.
--
-- The liability falls on MEMBERS -- the investors -- not on the directors. A knowing investor in a VCC whose resident
-- director has left loses limited liability for debts contracted after six months.
DECLARE Board HAS
    `has a director ordinarily resident in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has a director who is a director or representative of the manager` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the board` IS A Board
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the board meets section 48(1)` IF
        `the board`'s `has a director ordinarily resident in Singapore`
    AND `the board`'s `has a director who is a director or representative of the manager`

GIVEN `the board after resignation` IS A Board, `required to go by disqualification or removal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the resignation is valid` IF
        `the board meets section 48(1)` `the board after resignation`
    OR  `required to go by disqualification or removal`

DECLARE MemberExposure HAS
    `months trading without the required directors when the debt was contracted` IS A NUMBER
    `is a member` IS A BOOLEAN
    `knows the VCC is so trading` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the exposure` IS A MemberExposure
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the member is personally liable for the debt` IF
        `the exposure`'s `months trading without the required directors when the debt was contracted` GREATER THAN 6
    AND `the exposure`'s `is a member`
    AND `the exposure`'s `knows the VCC is so trading`

§§ `53 -- fit and proper directors`

-- s 53(2): the Registrar may direct removal of a director not fit and proper, after notice and a chance to show cause
-- (4), (5). (7): appeal to the Minister within 30 days; (8): the direction has effect pending the appeal.
GIVEN `an appeal is pending` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the removal direction has effect` IF
    TRUE

§§ `58 -- disqualification on conviction`

-- s 58(1): a person is disqualified if (a) convicted of (i) any offence, in Singapore OR ELSEWHERE, "involving fraud or
-- dishonesty and punishable with imprisonment for a term of 3 months or more", (ii) an offence under Part 12 of the
-- Securities and Futures Act, or (iii) specified money-laundering offences; (b) subject to an SFA s 232 civil penalty;
-- (c), (d) removed under SFA directions or conditions; or (e) subject to a prohibition order.
-- (3): must not act as director or take part in management. (4): 5 years -- from conviction if no imprisonment; from
-- RELEASE if imprisoned; from the penalty, direction or removal otherwise.
--
-- The test in (1)(a)(i) is the offence's MAXIMUM ("punishable with"), not the sentence: a fine for a fraud offence
-- carrying up to 3 months still disqualifies for 5 years.
DECLARE Conviction HAS
    `involves fraud or dishonesty` IS A BOOLEAN
    `maximum imprisonment in months` IS A NUMBER
    `was sentenced to imprisonment` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the conviction` IS A Conviction
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the conviction disqualifies` IF
        `the conviction`'s `involves fraud or dishonesty`
    AND `the conviction`'s `maximum imprisonment in months` AT LEAST 3

GIVEN `the conviction` IS A Conviction, `months since conviction` IS A NUMBER, `months since release` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is still disqualified` IF
        `the conviction disqualifies` `the conviction`
    AND (IF `the conviction`'s `was sentenced to imprisonment`
         THEN `months since release` LESS THAN 60
         ELSE `months since conviction` LESS THAN 60)
